 "caveats": [
  "SURVIVOR BIAS: survivors-only backtest universe, so CAGR is an UPPER BOUND. Of ~721 S&P names that left the index 2011-2026, only ~40 are genuine bankruptcies (the rest are M&A / ticker-changes, NOT losses) and are excluded from the panel. The failure-bias is bounded (momentum/quality screens avoid most pre-bankruptcy names) but real - not a survivorship-free track record.",
  "Backtested 2011-2026 on the BROAD universe (no floor; trading = eligible). Realistic forward ~22% net of cost + survivor haircut; per-2yr regime CAGR -9% to 48% (median 26%).",
  "Validated edge: top-5 monthly excess +1.0%%/mo, t 2.50 (SIGNIFICANT, persists/strengthens recently) \u2014 unlike the 1-month prediction, which is noise. Broad rank-IC is still ~0 (candidate-grade); the edge lives in the extreme top names.",
  "TACTICAL, not blind: the edge is strong near all-time highs / broad breadth and NEGATIVE in >10%% corrections. Deploy in healthy regimes; the PPI gauge takes the book to cash in drawdowns.",
  "TRADEABLE: low quarterly turnover (~165%/yr), negligible cost drag, and a $5M-ADV liquidity floor RAISES the CAGR (the edge is in liquid mid/large-caps, not microcaps).",
  "Decorrelated 0.40-0.45 from the other four sleeves; adds +0.14 to the deployable combined-book Sharpe (1.50 -> 1.64). Top-5 concentration = high single-name risk (115 distinct names rotated)."
 ]
